{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And behold, a smoking furnace.</b> Apparently it should have said והנה עשן תנור — 'and behold, smoke of a furnace' — just as is said of the theophany at Mount Sinai: ״ויעל עשנו כעשן הכבשן״." "<b>But</b> it is possible, by way of the Kabbalah, that the verse comes to make known to us this force that passed and received the offerings of Abraham, and that it possesses a masculine potency and a feminine potency: it possesses a masculine potency to produce effects, and a feminine potency in that it receives from outside itself, like this female who receives from the male, and all effects are magnified in it through its power. Therefore this force is called Shekhinah in the feminine, and Onkelos translated (Exodus 33:14) פני ילכו — 'My Face shall go' — as שכינתי תהך, and not יהך, and the name of this force is known." "<b>And there is</b> in this a rousing and a hint in the word תנור by the substitution of the ת״ו for the ט״ת (in the alphabet of א״ח ב״ז), and therefore it mentioned here תנור עשן — 'a smoking furnace' — which is the vessel that receives the fire, and this is a hint to the feminine potency, and לפיד אש — 'a flaming torch' — is the masculine potency, and this is why it is written אשר עבר — 'which passed' — in the singular, and did not say אשר עברו — 'which passed' — in the plural; and this is the language of ״כרת HaShem et Abram ברית״ — 'HaShem cut a covenant with Abram' — for the Shekhinah, which is the covenant, passed between the pieces." "<b>And know</b> that concerning this force it was mentioned above at the head of the parashah: ״ויבן שם מזבח ל-HaShem הנראה אליו״, and the discerning will understand."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:44.150869146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}